<title>USA: Inphynet restates earnings downward.</title>
<headline>Inphynet restates earnings downward.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>InPhynet Medical Management Inc has restated downward its 1996 year and 1997 first quarter earnings to reflect a change in accounting for the costs associated with its five-year pact with Physician Corp of America, MedPartners Inc said Wednesday.</p>
<p>As a result of the restatement, MedPartners and InPhyNet have adjusted the terms of their merger agreement.</p>
<p>InPhynet has restated its 1996 earnings to $0.81 a share from $1.04.</p>
<p>First quarter 1997 earnings were restated to $0.20 a share from $0.30.</p>
<p>Under the adjusted merger agreement, InPhynet holders will get 1.18 MedPartners shares for each InPhyNet share, instead of 1.311 MedPartners shares.</p>
</text>
